│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ sign_phase_line_compressor                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the heavily parameter-shared CRY-only line block with a more sign-sensitive       │
│                          │ hardware-efficient/line-compressor hybrid. The fixed RX feature map stores player sign    │
│                          │ primarily in the Y quadrature; adding trainable RZ followed by RY lets the circuit rotate │
│                          │ that sign information into Z readout. Independent per-wire RX/RZ/RY input rotations       │
│                          │ improve expressivity compared with the current orbit-shared decoder, while keeping        │
│                          │ post-readout rotations orbit-shared for regularization. Fixed CNOT line-compressor motifs │
│                          │ target tic-tac-toe line midpoints and the center using only allowed grid adjacencies,     │
│                          │ creating stronger non-parametric nonlinear/parity features than small-initialized         │
│                          │ controlled rotations. Shared CRY gates then softly route midpoint evidence into the       │
│                          │ measurement groups for cross/circle/draw without excessive parameters.                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
