│ patch_description        │ This proposal keeps the fixed data re-uploading, RX feature map, training loop, and       │
│                          │ measurement mapping unchanged, but replaces the heavy CNOT-compressor ansatz with a more  │
│                          │ symmetry-regularized line-phase kernel. It draws inspiration from the prior orbit-sharing │
│                          │ and tic-tac-toe line motifs, but uses a different mechanism: a D4-symmetric local phase   │
│                          │ decoder, a fixed CZ “interaction graph” over all legal adjacent grid edges, then          │
│                          │ trainable CRY line aggregators that softly collect endpoint evidence into row/column      │
│                          │ midpoints and the center. The design avoids the overly destructive bit-flip behavior of   │
│                          │ dense CNOT compression, reduces trainable parameters relative to the current program, and │
│                          │ aligns the final orbit-shared readout mixers with the fixed cross/edge, circle/corner,    │
│                          │ and draw/center observables.                                                              │
