│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ trainable_cry_line_features                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The current program scores poorly (test acc 0.25, essentially random) because its first   │
│                          │ layer is pure RZ rotations which commute trivially with the RX feature map and PauliZ     │
│                          │ measurements, contributing almost nothing. The CZ "kernel" on all 12 edges also adds      │
│                          │ depth without trainable signal extraction.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The best prior program (score 0.44) instead used trainable CRY entanglers on winning-line │
│                          │ segments plus center aggregation/broadcast, giving useful nonlinear features. I rebuild   │
│                          │ the block around that proven recipe while keeping the compact D4-orbit parameter sharing: │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Replace the leading RZ decoders with RY decoders (RY rotates the player-sign           │
│                          │ Y-quadrature info toward measurable Z) — this is the productive direction, unlike RZ.     │
│                          │ 2. Drop the heavy 12-edge CZ kernel (dead weight) and instead use trainable CRY           │
│                          │ entanglers along legal line segments (endpoint→midpoint), which directly build "two cells │
│                          │ agree on a line" features.                                                                │
│                          │ 3. Keep the center aggregation and center broadcast CRY motifs that worked in the 0.44    │
│                          │ program.                                                                                  │
│                          │ 4. Keep orbit-shared readout mixers (RY+RX) aligned with the measurement grouping.        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This keeps parameter count low (efficient) while restoring genuine trainable              │
│                          │ nonlinearity, which should lift accuracy well above the random baseline.                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
