│ patch_description        │ The current program's extra RX input layer (alongside RY) adds parameters without clear   │
│                          │ benefit and matched the weaker 90-param design. The strongest prior program (0.53) used:  │
│                          │ a single RY orbit-shared sign decoder, CRY line entanglers (endpoint→edge, pair→center,   │
│                          │ center→edge broadcast), and RY+RX orbit-shared readouts — 12 params/block, 72 total.      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I restore that proven compact structure but add one improvement: instead of having both   │
│                          │ `ry_corner_out` AND `rx_corner_out` as separate full readout layers, I keep the RY+RX     │
│                          │ readout (which the best program used) but tie the decoder to be RY-only (removing the     │
│                          │ wasteful RX input layer in the current code). This removes the 3 extra RX-input params    │
│                          │ (rx_corner_in/rx_edge_in/rx_center_in) per block that the current 0.44 program            │
│                          │ introduced, bringing us back to the efficient 12 params/block × 6 = 72 total              │
│                          │ configuration that scored 0.53.                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is parameter-efficient (fewer params, lower depth) and matches the architecture that │
│                          │ demonstrably generalized best.                                                            │
