│                          │ mini-batch steps per epoch, batch_size=15, l=3 data re-uploading, and p=2 ansatz          │
│                          │ repetitions per upload. The current ansatz is parameter-efficient but underfits: train    │
│                          │ accuracy is only about 0.43, suggesting that the circuit lacks strong nonlinear line      │
│                          │ features early in optimization.                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This proposal keeps the same inputs, outputs, data construction, optimizer, feature map,  │
│                          │ l, p, and measurements, but changes the ansatz block. The new block adds trainable RX     │
│                          │ sign decoders before entanglement, fixed CNOT line aggregators from endpoints to legal    │
│                          │ midpoint cells, and CRX/CRY controlled rotations. The CNOTs provide immediate             │
│                          │ non-parametric pair-product features instead of waiting for near-zero controlled-rotation │
│                          │ parameters to grow under Adam. CRX is aligned with the RX feature encoding and should     │
│                          │ improve player-sign sensitivity, while CRY mixers preserve the successful prior           │
│                          │ line-aggregation motif. Parameters remain orbit-shared for tic-tac-toe symmetry and       │
│                          │ efficiency, with 90 total parameters across all uploads/repeats.                          │
