                         Patch Metadata - Gen 14/30 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ line_aware_corner_edge_entangler                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ Building on the strongest prior ansatz (the orbit-shared RY decoder + CRY line-segment    │
│                          │ entangler that scored 0.53), I introduce a richer but still parameter-efficient and       │
│                          │ symmetry-aware entangling scheme.                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key insights:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. The fixed measurements group corners→circle, edges→cross, center→draw. Winning lines   │
│                          │ couple a corner, an edge, and either the center or another corner. So the decisive        │
│                          │ correlations are *corner↔edge* and *edge↔center*. The prior ansatz only routed            │
│                          │ corner→edge (CRY ) one direction. I add the reverse edge→corner direction with its own    │
│                          │ shared parameter, giving the circuit bidirectional information flow along every grid edge │
│                          │ — this directly implements the recommended "diagonal two-cell correlation" motif using    │
│                          │ the corner↔edge adjacency.                                                                │
│                          │ 2. I add a layer of RZ rotations *between* the entanglers. After CRY gates rotate         │
│                          │ amplitude out of the Y-quadrature into accessible directions, a trainable RZ can re-phase │
│                          │ and (combined with the surrounding RY) build genuinely 3-axis local frames, increasing    │
│                          │ expressivity per qubit at the cost of only 3 shared parameters (corner/edge/center        │
│                          │ orbits).                                                                                  │
│                          │ 3. Center↔edge bidirectional CRY (already present one way) is kept and balanced so the    │
│                          │ draw readout (z[8]) gets line context and broadcasts back.                                │
│                          │ 4. All gates are shared by D4 board orbit (corner/edge/center), keeping the per-block     │
│                          │ parameter count low (12 unique params → 72 total, same budget as the best prior) while    │
│                          │ increasing the effective entangling structure and the local rotation rank. This preserves │
│                          │ the small train-test gap while raising accuracy.                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The block structure per upload-repeat is:                                                 │
│                          │ RY decode → CRY corner→edge → CRY edge→corner → CRY edge→center → CRY center→edge → mid   │
│                          │ RZ orbit phases → RY readout → RX readout.                                                │
