                         Patch Metadata - Gen 15/30 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_pre_entangle_rz_and_full_edge_cry                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses only RY single-qubit rotations and CRY on a subset of edges. The  │
│                          │ model is underfitting (train acc 0.43 < val 0.56), so we need more expressivity per block │
│                          │ while staying parameter-efficient.                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Two targeted changes:                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Add a trainable RZ phase layer right after the RY decode layer. Although RZ commutes   │
│                          │ with the Z readout *at the end*, here it sits before the CRY entanglers, where it rotates │
│                          │ amplitude in the X-Y plane before entanglement. This gives each qubit a genuine 2-axis    │
│                          │ local frame (RY then RZ) before mixing, adding only 3 shared params (corner/edge/center   │
│                          │ orbits).                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Use the *full set* of adjacent grid edges for the perimeter CRY entanglers (currently  │
│                          │ only one direction per edge). Adding the missing perimeter directions (1->0, 1->2, 3->2,  │
│                          │ 3->4, 5->4, 5->6, 7->6, 7->0) under a separate shared parameter doubles the perimeter     │
│                          │ information flow (bidirectional coupling along each winning-line segment) at the cost of  │
│                          │ just 1 new shared parameter.                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Together this raises N_PARAMS_PER_BLOCK from 12 to 16 (N_PARAMS 72->96), still well       │
│                          │ within budget, and should improve fitting capacity and reduce loss while respecting D4    │
│                          │ symmetry and adjacency constraints.                                                       │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.2099                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-opus-4.8                                                      │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ diff_summary             │ added: 22; deleted: 0; modified: 0;                                                       │
