│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ distinct_per_orbit_entanglers_with_pre_phase                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz shares a single parameter across all 8 perimeter CRY gates, all 4      │
│                          │ center-aggregator CRY gates, and all 4 center-broadcast CRY gates. While                  │
│                          │ symmetry-inspired, this over-sharing severely limits expressivity (train accuracy is only │
│                          │ 0.43, indicating underfitting). The key insight from the prior programs is that           │
│                          │ distinguishing the perimeter segments by *direction* (endpoint→mid vs mid→endpoint) and   │
│                          │ adding a pre-entanglement phase layer raised expressivity.                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit:                                                                                │
│                          │ 1. Splits the single perimeter `cry_pair_to_edge` into two directional families           │
│                          │ (endpoint→mid and mid→endpoint), giving bidirectional coupling along winning-line         │
│                          │ segments — the strongest motif from prior top circuits.                                   │
│                          │ 2. Adds a lightweight orbit-shared RZ pre-entanglement phase layer (only 3 params) so     │
│                          │ each qubit has a 2-axis frame before the CRY mixers, which does not commute through them  │
│                          │ (unlike a terminal RZ near a Z readout).                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This adds only ~5 params per block (72 → ~102 total), keeping us within the gate budget   │
│                          │ while substantially raising expressivity to close the underfitting gap.                   │
