                         Patch Metadata - Gen 17/30 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_diagonal_corner_to_center_entanglers                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz only couples corners to their adjacent edges and edges to the center.  │
│                          │ But the two diagonal winning lines (0,8,4) and (2,8,6) directly connect corners to the    │
│                          │ center. The grid adjacency allows corner-center coupling only via edges, but in fact the  │
│                          │ legal edge set does NOT contain corner-center edges, so we must route diagonal info       │
│                          │ differently.                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Instead, I add a dedicated trainable corner→edge "diagonal context" CRY layer that        │
│                          │ distinguishes the two diagonals from the rows/columns by using a *separate* shared        │
│                          │ parameter (`cry_diag_context`). The diagonal lines pass through specific                  │
│                          │ corner-edge-center paths. Since corners (0,2,4,6) each sit on exactly one diagonal        │
│                          │ through the center, and the center is reached via edges, I strengthen the center's        │
│                          │ diagonal sensitivity by adding a second, independently-parametrized center→edge broadcast │
│                          │ that uses a distinct parameter from the existing one. This breaks the over-sharing of the │
│                          │ single `cry_center_to_mid` parameter and gives the model more expressivity for the draw   │
│                          │ class (which is the hardest to separate), at the cost of just 1 extra parameter per block │
│                          │ (6 total).                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is a low-cost, symmetry-respecting expressivity boost targeting the diagonal         │
│                          │ patterns that the current line-segment-only entanglers cannot represent. It also reduces  │
│                          │ parameter over-sharing that may be limiting train accuracy (currently only 0.43).         │
