│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ revert_and_split_entangler_orbits                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The added RX pre-shift layer hurt performance (0.44 vs 0.53). I revert to the stronger    │
│                          │ prior block (RY decode, CRY entanglers, RY/RX readout) and then apply the suggested       │
│                          │ orbit-split: the single shared `cry_endpoint_to_mid` is split into horizontal-edge and    │
│                          │ vertical-edge keys, and `cry_mid_to_center`/`cry_center_to_mid` are split into row vs.    │
│                          │ column keys. This lets the circuit independently weight row and column line correlations  │
│                          │ (tic-tac-toe rows and columns are distinct winning lines), addressing underfitting with   │
│                          │ only a modest parameter increase, while keeping D4-respecting orbit sharing for           │
│                          │ efficiency.                                                                               │
