│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ restore_cry_motif_with_dual_decode                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The current candidate (score 0.45) regressed below the prior best (0.53) because it added │
│                          │ non-parametric CNOT line aggregators and CRX gates that scramble the Y-quadrature         │
│                          │ encoding before the trainable layers can decode the player sign. The fixed CNOTs create   │
│                          │ strong fixed entanglement that the limited shared params cannot undo, lowering even train │
│                          │ accuracy to 0.33.                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I revert to the proven CRY-based motif of the prior best (72-param, score 0.53) but keep  │
│                          │ a useful improvement: separate RX-sign + RY-decode local layers (sign-sensitive decode)   │
│                          │ which align with the RX feature map. I remove all fixed CNOTs (they were the regression   │
│                          │ cause) and replace the CRX entanglers with CRY (which empirically worked best in the      │
│                          │ prior champions). This keeps parameter count efficient (~84) while restoring the          │
│                          │ expressive, symmetry-respecting line-segment structure. The combination of a learnable RX │
│                          │ offset plus the CRY line entanglers should both fit better and generalize, targeting the  │
│                          │ 0.53+ regime.                                                                             │
