                         Patch Metadata - Gen 20/30 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ direct_winline_readout_decoder                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ A fundamentally different design philosophy. The prior ansätze over-relied on heavy       │
│                          │ bidirectional CRY entanglement that destroyed the clean sign-information stored by the RX │
│                          │ feature map, collapsing accuracy (the current 96-param version got *worse*, 37%, than the │
│                          │ 72-param seeds at 52%).                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key insight: the RX(±2π/3) feature map writes player sign into the Y-quadrature. The      │
│                          │ cleanest classifier reads it back as Z via a single trainable RY layer, then needs ONLY   │
│                          │ enough entanglement to compute "three-in-a-line agreement" — the actual decision function │
│                          │ of tic-tac-toe. Excessive entanglement is harmful: it scrambles the already-informative   │
│                          │ single-qubit signal.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ New strategy:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. **Per-orbit RY decoder** (sign → Z), as before, but immediately followed by a          │
│                          │ per-orbit RX phase to give a 2-axis local frame *without* RZ (RZ commutes through Z       │
│                          │ readout and wastes capacity — confirmed by prior notes).                                  │
│                          │ 2. **Single light directional entangling pass** along winning-line segments (endpoint →   │
│                          │ midpoint only, no reverse pass) using ONE shared CRY parameter. This injects              │
│                          │ "two-cells-agree" features at minimal depth.                                              │
│                          │ 3. **Center coupling** with one shared CRY from the four edges into the center, giving    │
│                          │ the draw readout (qubit 8) explicit middle-row/column context — and a separate single     │
│                          │ shared center→edge broadcast so diagonal/center evidence reaches the perimeter readouts   │
│                          │ within the re-uploading repeats.                                                          │
│                          │ 4. **Per-orbit readout RY** aligned to the measurement grouping.                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This keeps the parameter count LOW (≈11 per block → 66 total, fewer than the failing 96), │
│                          │ keeps depth shallow (one entangling sweep instead of three), preserves the informative    │
│                          │ feature signal, and lets data re-uploading (l=3, p=2) build up the line-agreement         │
│                          │ nonlinearity across repetitions rather than within one over-deep block.                   │
